  "body": "### What is the issue with the MIME Sniffing Standard?\n\nIn the vint parsing algorithm (https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-a-vint), two of the steps appear to be backwards. Step four states: \n> 4. While number size is less than max vint length, and less than length, continuously loop through these steps: \n    1. If the sequence[index] & mask is not zero, abort these steps.\n    2. Let mask be the value of mask >> 1.\n    3. Increment number size by one\n\nBut index is not mentioned and set to zero until step 5:\n> 5. Let index be 0.\n\nIt seems that steps 4 and 5 should swap places.\n",
